    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Overview</span>
      <h2>What are TM44 inspections?</h2>
      <p>Air conditioning inspections are a mandatory requirement designed to ensure that AC systems perform efficiently. This is contained in the revised Energy Performance of Buildings Directive (EPBD), progressively implemented from January 2007, and is now a requirement in England and Wales, Scotland and Northern Ireland.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">Scope</span>
      <h2>What it covers</h2>
      <p>All air conditioning systems with an output of more than 12kW require an inspection at intervals not exceeding five years – but in Scotland this can be as little as three years if systems are assessed as poorly maintained and inefficient.</p>
      <p>Inspections must be carried out to CIBSE TM44, which sets out the qualifications required by assessors and the inspection process. Inspectors must also make recommendations to improve the efficiency of the plant.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

